## 4. Seeded failure — secret scan (real control, real scanner)

A fixture containing a fake GitHub-token shape was written outside the repository and scanned with
the repository's own scanner.

```text
$ node scripts/secret-scan.mjs "C:\Users\HP\AppData\Local\Temp\opencode\seeded-secret.txt"
secret-scan: blocked - possible credential(s) detected

  C:\Users\HP\AppData\Local\Temp\opencode\seeded-secret.txt:2  [github-token]

Remove the value, rotate it if it was ever real, and commit again.
This is a local guard, not a substitute for provider-side scanning.

(exit 1)
```

The fixture was deleted immediately after the run. The scanner over the staged working set is clean;
see the final scan output recorded in the commit evidence.

